# Navbar — Contact IconButton alignment (mobile)

When editing `Navbar.tsx` or the navbar skeleton, **never** reintroduce the 1px-short contact column bug.

## Root cause

- `<header>` has `border-b` on mobile (`md:border-b-0` on desktop).
- An extra `border-b` on the mobile contact wrapper steals 1px from the flex child (`border-box`) → button background is 55px vs navbar 56px.

## Required pattern (mobile `< md`)

1. Header row: `items-stretch` + `min-h-[56px]`.
2. Contact wrapper: `flex shrink-0 self-stretch md:hidden border-l border-indigo-100` — **no `border-b`** on mobile.
3. Contact `Button` (icon): `box-border h-full! min-h-[56px]! w-[56px]!` + `icon-24-mobile`.
4. Skeleton right slot: `h-full min-h-[56px] w-[56px]`, same border rules as live UI.

## Desktop (`md+`)

- Contact text wrapper may use `border-l border-b border-indigo-100`.
- Button: `min-h-[48px]!` / `min-[1266px]:min-h-[72px]!` to match header tokens.

## Before finishing

- [ ] Mobile contact div has no standalone `border-b` (only header draws bottom edge on mobile).
- [ ] No `h-[54px]` / `h-[55px]` on contact slot.
- [ ] Full spec: `CLAUDE.md` §8.5.1
